Acceptance tests you must satisfy:
     1. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': 'Feed the checker a transition function that dispatches on an enum-typed status and, in one branch, calls Transport().complete(...) directly before finishing the transition. The checker should report this function as a violation.', 'proves': 'Proves the rule rejects an edge body that directly makes an LLM/subprocess call, the core motivating case from the exo-2e2 and exo-d1b.2 incidents.', 'restatement_span_id': 's1', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': 'from enum import Enum\n\nclass Status(Enum):\n    NEEDS_SPEC = 1\n    READY = 2\n\ndef integrate_edge(status: Status, ctx):\n    if status == Status.NEEDS_SPEC:\n        result = Transport().complete(prompt="derive spec")\n        ctx.mark_integrated(result)\n    elif status == Status.READY:\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c1'}
     2. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': 'Feed the checker the same transition function, but with the LLM call replaced by writing a marker to the bus and returning immediately. The checker should report no violation.', 'proves': 'Proves the rule allows the correct pattern — emitting a durable marker and yielding — inside an edge body.', 'restatement_span_id': 's2', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': 'from enum import Enum\n\nclass Status(Enum):\n    NEEDS_SPEC = 1\n    READY = 2\n\ndef integrate_edge(status: Status, ctx):\n    if status == Status.NEEDS_SPEC:\n        ctx.bus.write_marker("needs_spec_bounce")\n        return\n    elif status == Status.READY:\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': False}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c2'}
     3. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': "Feed the checker a plain helper function, with no enum dispatch and no edge marker comment, that calls Transport().complete(...) directly. The checker should not flag it because the function isn't recognized as a transition body.", 'proves': 'Proves the rule only applies to functions it can identify as edges, not to every function that contains an unbounded call.', 'restatement_span_id': 's3', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': 'def helper_utility(ctx):\n    result = Transport().complete(prompt="derive spec")\n    return result\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': False}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c3'}
     4. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': "Feed the checker a helper function that has no enum dispatch but is annotated with the comment '# asp-fsm: edge' and embeds a direct Transport().complete(...) call. The checker should flag it.", 'proves': 'Proves the opt-in marker-comment way of identifying an edge body works on its own, independent of the enum-dispatch heuristic.', 'restatement_span_id': 's4', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': '# asp-fsm: edge\ndef dispatch_helper(ctx):\n    result = Transport().complete(prompt="derive spec")\n    return result\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c4'}
     5. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': "Feed the checker a transition function that dispatches on an enum-typed status and, in one branch, calls another FSM's run(...) method directly before finishing the transition. The checker should report this as a violation.", 'proves': "Proves the rule rejects an edge body that calls another FSM's run/drive entrypoint.", 'restatement_span_id': 's5', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': 'from enum import Enum\n\nclass Status(Enum):\n    NEEDS_SPEC = 1\n    READY = 2\n\ndef integrate_edge(status: Status, ctx):\n    if status == Status.NEEDS_SPEC:\n        SpecifyMachine().run(ctx)\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n    elif status == Status.READY:\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c5'}
     6. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': "Feed the checker a transition function that dispatches on an enum-typed status and, in one branch, runs a 'while True' retry loop before finishing the transition. The checker should report this as a violation.", 'proves': 'Proves the rule rejects an edge body containing an unbounded retry/convergence loop.', 'restatement_span_id': 's6', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': 'from enum import Enum\n\nclass Status(Enum):\n    NEEDS_SPEC = 1\n    READY = 2\n\ndef integrate_edge(status: Status, ctx):\n    if status == Status.NEEDS_SPEC:\n        while True:\n            if ctx.try_converge():\n                break\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n    elif status == Status.READY:\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c6'}
     7. {'type': 'behavior', 'description': "Feed the checker a transition function that dispatches on an enum-typed status, where the branch calls a separate helper function, and it's that helper (not the transition function itself) that makes the direct LLM call. The checker should not flag the transition function.", 'proves': 'Proves the documented limitation holds: indirection through a helper function defeats detection, so the rule flags only direct calls inside the identified edge body.', 'restatement_span_id': 's7', 'when': {'interpreter': 'python3', 'script': 'scripts/check_edge_duration.py', 'args': [], 'stdin': 'from enum import Enum\n\nclass Status(Enum):\n    NEEDS_SPEC = 1\n    READY = 2\n\ndef _call_llm(ctx):\n    return Transport().complete(prompt="derive spec")\n\ndef integrate_edge(status: Status, ctx):\n    if status == Status.NEEDS_SPEC:\n        result = _call_llm(ctx)\n        ctx.mark_integrated(result)\n    elif status == Status.READY:\n        ctx.mark_integrated(None)\n'}, 'then': [{'observe': 'stdout_json', 'field': 'flagged', 'op': 'eq', 'value': False}], 'max_runs': 1, 'timeout_seconds': 10, 'clause_id': 'c7'}

When the task is done, complete it through the typed-handoff contract (do NOT open a pull request — the exophial reducer integrates your branch itself once the handoff is valid):

